  <p class="eyebrow">Public EV charging study</p>
  <h1>Bull Run Library</h1>
  <p class="where">public library · Prince William County</p>

  <div class="answer">
    <p>Nothing is being built here.</p>
    <p>This site is one of twelve being <strong>studied</strong> for whether public electric
       vehicle charging could work here one day. No charger has been approved, funded,
       designed, or scheduled — and this study cannot approve one.</p>
    <p>You tapped a tag placed by a George Mason University student fellowship team doing
       that study.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What the study says about this site</h2>
  <dl class="figures">
    <div><dt>Chargers that might make sense to start with</dt><dd>2</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Space worth leaving room for, long term</dt><dd>up to 4</dd></div>
    <div><dt>How confident we are in the data here</dt><dd>Low</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Is the electrical capacity confirmed?</dt><dd>No — placeholder</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <div class="caveat">
    <strong>The most important thing on this page:</strong> nobody has confirmed that the
    electrical service here could actually support chargers. That figure is a
    <strong>placeholder</strong> — a stand-in used so the study could be completed — and it
    is a placeholder at <strong>all twelve</strong> sites. Confirming it needs the building's
    electrical records and the utility, and that work has not been done.
  </div>

  <h2>What this can and cannot tell you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>It can</strong> help compare sites and decide which are worth looking at first.</li>
    <li><strong>It cannot</strong> approve, permit, or fund anything.</li>
    <li><strong>It is not</strong> an engineering design, a utility confirmation, a fire or
        accessibility review, or a commitment by any government.</li>
    <li>The demand figures are modelled, not measured. No one has counted real charging here.</li>
    <li>Costs are early screening estimates for comparison, never budgets or quotes.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="actions">
